  "engine_note": "This version is genuinely machine-executable, not documentation. classify_incidents.py loads this file and evaluates gate_conditions/supporting_evidence directly -- no thresholds are hardcoded in Python anymore. Condition trees use {'field','op','value'} leaves combined via {'all':[...]}, {'any':[...]}, {'not': ...}. 'not_computable': true always evaluates False. Fields referenced here are the flat feature names computed once per incident (see FEATURE_FIELDS in classify_incidents.py) -- not raw incidents-file paths, since several (own_radio_normal, mimo_pattern, not_mobility, etc.) are derived combinations needed by more than one rule.",
  "id_scheme": "Each rule's id matches the same id (or parent_id, for a subcategory's gate) in causes.json and solutions.json.",
  "kpi_threshold_reference": {
    "rsrp_dbm": {
      "poor": "< -110",
      "fair": "[-110, -100)",
      "good": "[-100, -90)",
      "excellent": ">= -90"
    },
    "sinr_db": {
      "poor": "< 0",
      "fair": "[0, 10)",
      "good": "[10, 15)",
      "excellent": ">= 15"
    },
    "rsrq_db": {
      "poor": "< -20",
      "fair": "[-20, -15)",
      "good": "[-15, -10)",
      "excellent": ">= -10"
    },
    "cqi_0_15": {
      "poor_qpsk": "1-6",
      "fair_16qam": "7-9",
      "good_64_256qam": "10-15"
    },
    "mcs_0_28": {
      "poor": "0-9",
      "fair": "10-16",
      "good": "17-28+"
    },
    "bler_pct": {
      "high": "> 10"
    },
    "prb_rb_utilization_pct": {
      "congested": ">= 80"
    },
    "cell_edge_rsrp_dbm": {
      "threshold": "< -100"
    },
    "ping_pong_dwell_time_s": {
      "threshold": "< 5"
    },
    "handover_a3_gap_db": {
      "threshold": "< -6"
    },
    "high_speed_kmh": {
      "threshold": ">= 50"
    },
    "outage_near_zero_throughput_mbps": {
      "threshold": "< 0.05 (absolute floor, not a percentile)"
    },
    "universal_demand_precondition_mbps": {
      "threshold": "expected_tp > 0.1 -- checked before every category"
    }
  },
  "evaluation_instructions": [
    "Evaluate rules in priority order ascending (already sorted below).",
    "Universal precondition (demand_confirmed_broad) is checked once, outside this rule list, before any rule is evaluated.",
    "For a plain rule: evaluate gate_conditions with gate_logic (ALL/ANY). If satisfied, the rule fires with parent_id as the result.",
    "For a rule with 'alternatives' (Mobility's C08 only): first confirm the outer gate_conditions, then evaluate each entry in 'alternatives' IN ORDER; the first one whose own condition is true becomes the result id (not the parent_id) -- these are peer patterns, not parent+evidence.",
    "Once a rule/alternative fires, independently evaluate every 'supporting_evidence' entry and attach the ids of every one that is also true.",
    "Stop at the first rule (in priority order) that fires. If nothing fires through C13, check C14 then C15."
  ],
